oe":18,"roa":10.8,"moat":{"ticker":"IT","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Gartner 在資訊科技研究與顧問領域建立了強大的品牌聲譽，這使其能夠收取高額的服務費用。客戶高度依賴 Gartner 的報告和分析來做出關鍵的技術決策，這種依賴性轉化為其定價權。雖然存在其他研究機構，但 Gartner 的市場領導地位和品牌信任度構成了顯著的壁壘，使其能夠維持較高的利潤率，並在一定程度上轉嫁成本。","comment_en":"Gartner commands a strong brand reputation in IT research and advisory, enabling premium pricing. Clients heavily rely on Gartner's reports and analysis for critical technology decisions, translating into pricing power. While competitors exist, Gartner's market leadership and brand trust form a significant barrier, allowing it to maintain healthy margins and pass on costs to some extent."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"IT 產業的資訊研究和顧問服務領域，專利和監管壁壘相對較低。Gartner 的核心競爭力在於其研究方法、數據庫和分析師的專業知識，這些難以透過專利保護。雖然有版權保護其報告內容，但這並非嚴格意義上的專利壁壘。行業監管也較少，因此這方面護城河非常薄弱。","comment_en":"The IT research and advisory sector has relatively low barriers from patents and regulation. Gartner's core strengths lie in its methodologies, databases, and analyst expertise, which are difficult to protect via patents. While copyrights protect its reports, these are not strict patent-like barriers. Regulatory oversight is also minimal, making this a very weak moat dimension."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"客戶對 Gartner 的依賴性是其轉換成本的主要來源。企業將 Gartner 的研究報告和分析整合到其戰略規劃、採購決策和技術路線圖中。更換供應商不僅意味著尋找替代品，還需要重新學習、驗證新數據，並可能影響關鍵業務決策的準確性。這種深度整合和對數據連續性的需求，使得客戶轉換成本高昂。","comment_en":"Client dependency on Gartner is the primary source of switching costs. Enterprises integrate Gartner's research and analysis into their strategic planning, procurement decisions, and technology roadmaps. Switching vendors involves not just finding alternatives but also relearning, validating new data, and potentially impacting the accuracy of critical business decisions. This deep integration and need for data continuity create high switching costs for clients."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Gartner 的網絡效應相對有限。雖然其研究報告的廣泛使用可能間接帶來一些聲譽效應，但並非典型的網絡效應，即用戶越多，產品或服務價值越高的情況。其價值主要來自於獨立的研究和分析，而非用戶之間的互動。客戶購買的是信息和洞察，而不是參與一個不斷增長的用戶網絡。","comment_en":"Gartner's network effects are relatively limited. While the widespread use of its research reports might indirectly create some reputational effects, it's not a typical network effect where more users increase the value of the product or service. Its value stems primarily from independent research and analysis, not user-to-user interaction. Clients purchase information and insights, not participation in a growing user network."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Gartner 在 IT 研究領域的規模使其能夠收集和處理大量數據，並聘請頂尖分析師，從而產生更深入、更全面的報告。這種規模經濟有助於降低單份報告的平均生產成本，並增強其研究的權威性。相較於小型競爭對手，Gartner 的規模使其在數據獲取和人才吸引方面具有成本優勢。","comment_en":"Gartner's scale in IT research allows it to gather and process vast amounts of data and attract top analysts, leading to more in-depth and comprehensive reports. This economies of scale helps reduce the average production cost per report and enhances the authority of its research. Compared to smaller competitors, Gartner's size provides a cost advantage in data acquisition and talent attraction."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Gartner 的業務模式並不依賴於獨特的地理位置或實體資產。其核心價值在於知識、數據和分析能力，這些可以在全球範圍內複製和擴展。雖然其客戶遍布全球，但並不存在特定地理區域的壟斷性資產，使其在這方面的護城河非常薄弱。","comment_en":"Gartner's business model does not rely on unique geographical locations or physical assets. Its core value lies in knowledge, data, and analytical capabilities, which can be replicated and scaled globally. While its client base is global, there are no monopolistic assets tied to specific geographic regions, making this a very weak moat dimension."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Gartner 在其運營效率方面表現出色，體現在其能夠持續產生穩定的自由現金流（FCF TTM: $1,288.9M）和健康的 ROE (18.0%) 及 ROA (10.8%)。這表明公司有效地管理其成本結構，並將資源轉化為利潤。其 F-Score 為 7/9，也顯示出良好的財務健康狀況和運營穩健性。","comment_en":"Gartner demonstrates strong operational efficiency, reflected in its consistent generation of robust free cash flow (FCF TTM: $1,288.9M) and healthy ROE (18.0%) and ROA (10.8%). This indicates effective management of its cost structure and efficient conversion of resources into profits. Its F-Score of 7/9 further suggests good financial health and operational stability."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Gartner 的資本配置策略似乎是穩健的。公司在維持健康的資產負債表（現金 $1,488.7M / 負債 $2,979.3M）的同時，持續回購股票並進行戰略性收購，以擴展其服務範圍和市場影響力。其 ROE 和 ROA 表明資本配置能夠產生不錯的回報，但仍有進一步優化的空間。","comment_en":"Gartner's capital allocation strategy appears sound. The company maintains a healthy balance sheet (Cash $1,488.7M / Debt $2,979.3M) while consistently engaging in share repurchases and strategic acquisitions to expand its service offerings and market reach. Its ROE and ROA indicate that capital allocation generates decent returns, though there may be room for further optimization."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"如轉換成本部分所述，客戶對 Gartner 的依賴性極高，這直接轉化為極高的客戶留存率。一旦企業將 Gartner 的研究和分析納入其運營流程，就很少會輕易更換。這種持續的客戶關係為公司提供了穩定的收入來源和可預測的現金流，是其重要的護城河。","comment_en":"As discussed under switching costs, clients exhibit high dependency on Gartner, directly translating into very strong customer retention. Once enterprises integrate Gartner's research and analysis into their operational workflows, they are unlikely to switch easily. This sustained client relationship provides a stable revenue stream and predictable cash flow, forming a significant moat."},"m10_durability":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Gartner 的業務模式具有相當的持久性。儘管科技行業變化迅速，但企業對獨立、權威的 IT 市場洞察和戰略建議的需求將持續存在。Gartner 的品牌聲譽、客戶關係和研究能力使其能夠適應行業變化，並在可預見的未來繼續保持其市場地位。其核心價值不易被顛覆。","comment_en":"Gartner's business model possesses considerable durability. Despite the rapid pace of technological change, the need for independent, authoritative IT market insights and strategic advice will persist. Gartner's brand reputation, client relationships, and research capabilities enable it to adapt to industry shifts and maintain its market position for the foreseeable future. Its core value is not easily disrupted."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Gartner 在資訊科技研究領域築起了堅固的護城河，主要體現為極高的客戶轉換成本和強大的品牌定價權。客戶將 Gartner 的分析深度整合到其業務決策中，使得更換供應商的成本高昂且風險較大。其規模經濟帶來了成本優勢和研究的權威性，進而鞏固了其市場領導地位。雖然網絡效應和專利壁壘較弱，但其穩健的運營效率、持續的客戶留存以及業務模式的持久性，使其成為一個具有特許經營性質的資訊服務提供者，能夠持續產生穩定的現金流。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Gartner possesses a robust moat in the IT research sector, primarily driven by high customer switching costs and strong brand pricing power. Clients deeply integrate Gartner's analysis into their business decisions, making vendor changes costly and risky. Economies of scale provide cost advantages and research authority, reinforcing its market leadership. While network effects and patent barriers are weak, its solid operational efficiency, consistent customer retention, and business model durability position it as a franchise-like information service provider capable of generating stable cash flows.","evidenceHash":"ae625c1b732c5784510e9f7d5a5d987bc95f33c42501dd69c2e63222a6711332","assessmentPolicy":"us-buffett-moat-v3"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":7,"checkedAt":null}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/IT.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/IT.png","website":"https://www.gartner.com","ceo":"Eugene A. Hall","full_time_employees":"19285","description":"Gartner, Inc. functions as a premier research and advisory enterprise, extending its reach across the United States, Canada, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and various international markets. Its operations are structured into three main divisions: Research, Conferences, and Consulting. The Research division primarily offers a subscription service, enabling on-demand access to extensive published studies, data, industry benchmarks, and direct consultations with its expert network. The Conferences segment provides a platform for business professionals to acquire new knowledge, share insights, and foster connections. Lastly, the Consulting segment furnishes clients with market research, bespoke analyses, and direct, on-site support services. This segment specifically addresses critical IT challenges, offering practical strategies for areas such as optimizing IT expenditures, managing digital transformation, and enhancing IT sourcing processes. Founded in 1979, Gartner, Inc. has its corporate base in Stamford, Connecticut.","description_en":"Gartner, Inc. functions as a premier research and advisory enterprise, extending its reach across the United States, Canada, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and various international markets. Its operations are structured into three main divisions: Research, Conferences, and Consulting. The Research division primarily offers a subscription service, enabling on-demand access to extensive published studies, data, industry benchmarks, and direct consultations with its expert network. The Conferences segment provides a platform for business professionals to acquire new knowledge, share insights, and foster connections. Lastly, the Consulting segment furnishes clients with market research, bespoke analyses, and direct, on-site support services. This segment specifically addresses critical IT challenges, offering practical strategies for areas such as optimizing IT expenditures, managing digital transformation, and enhancing IT sourcing processes. Founded in 1979, Gartner, Inc. has its corporate base in Stamford, Connecticut.","description_zh":"**Gartner, Inc. (IT) 業務營運精煉**\n\nGartner, Inc. 是一家領先的全球性研究與顧問機構，業務遍及美國、加拿大、歐洲、中東、非洲及其他國際市場。公司營運主要劃分為三大事業群：研究（Research）、會議（Conferences）及顧問（Consulting）。\n\n「研究」事業群提供訂閱式服務，讓客戶能即時獲取豐富的研究報告、數據、產業標竿分析，並可直接諮詢其專家團隊。此部分是 Gartner 的核心業務，旨在提供前瞻性的市場洞察與決策支援。\n\n「會議」事業群則搭建平台，匯聚產業專業人士交流新知、分享見解並拓展人脈。\n\n「顧問」事業群則針對客戶的特定 IT 挑戰，提供客製化的市場研究、專案分析及現場支援服務。此業務專注於協助客戶解決關鍵 IT 問題，例如優化 IT 支出、推動數位轉型策略，以及改善 IT 採購流程。\n\nGartner 成立於 1979 年，總部位於美國康乃狄克州史丹佛。","address":"56 Top Gallant Road","city":"Stamford","state":"CT","zip":"06902-7700","country":"US","phone":"203 316 1111","full_address":"56 Top Gallant Road, Stamford, CT 06902-7700, US","range_52w":"124.25-257.69","year_high":257.69,"year_low":124.25,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":124.25,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Rupani Altaf","title":"officer: EVP, Chief Information Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":165,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Rupani Altaf","title":"officer: EVP, Chief Information Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"F-InKind","shares":60,"price":207.31,"total_val":0.01},{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"Rupani Altaf","title":"officer: EVP, Chief Information Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":165,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"FERGUSON DIANA SUE","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"J-Other","shares":139,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"FERGUSON DIANA SUE","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":139,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"FERGUSON DIANA SUE","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"J-Other","shares":139,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"PAGLIUCA STEPHEN G","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"J-Other","shares":130,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"PAGLIUCA STEPHEN G","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":130,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"PAGLIUCA STEPHEN G","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"J-Other","shares":130,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Rus Daniela L","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":126,"price":0,"total_val":0}],"stock_splits":[{"date":"1996-04-01","ratio":"2 : 1","desc":"供應商報告的股數調整比例；未獨立核實事件類型。","type":"FMP 股數調整"},{"date":"1995-06-29","ratio":"2 : 1","desc":"供應商報告的股數調整比例；未獨立核實事件類型。","type":"FMP 股數調整"},{"date":"1994-08-29","ratio":"2 : 1","desc":"供應商報告的股數調整比例；未獨立核實事件類型。","type":"FMP 股數調整"}],"fmp_symbol":"IT","real_5y_prices":[],"historical_dcf_series":[],"name_en":"Gartner, Inc.","expansion":{"status":"available","capturedAt":"2026-10-22T14:18:11.631Z","reason":null,"detailPath":"cache/us_companies/IT.json"}},"snapshot":null,"model":null}
